# inter.face

This repo is the inter.face design pipeline: art direction for any interface —
web, mobile, tablet, or desktop, page-shaped or tool-shaped. To run it, read
AGENTS.md and PRINCIPLES.md, collect the inbox into runs/<slug>/inbox/ (reference
images, links with a line each, brand assets, the brand book if one exists),
settle the surface class first (TRANSLATE.md row 1, no safe default), then run
loops/01-direction.md to Gate A, loops/02-craft.md to Gate B, and
loops/03-system.md to Gate C, stopping at all three for the human. Three rules are
hard and never skip: accessible by default, keyboard completeness on tool-shaped
surfaces, and human gates as real stops. The deliverable is DIRECTION.md,
tokens.json, one comp per surface — coded by default, a generated image when the
run opts in — the navigable board those comps are reviewed on, one measured
prototype per technique, and a component sheet built from the tokens alone. The
pipeline stops before code. Close the run through IMPROVE.md: ask once, show the
payload, default to no. Never publish past a gate without a human decision.
